{
  "description": "CRYPTO_SPEC §6.6: head attestation (Ed25519). head_attestation_signed_bytes = LP(\"<suite>/head-attestation\", project_id, attester_user_id, chain_head_hash_hex, chain_head_seq). The chain and keys reference the canonical chain in chain-entries.json (24 entries — only the hashes changed, following the 2026-09-14 ES + PF1 full regeneration; the meaning of the positive/negative cases is unchanged)",
  "signed_fields_order": [
    "domain",
    "project_id",
    "attester_user_id",
    "chain_head_hash_hex",
    "chain_head_seq"
  ],
  "binary_encoding": "The chain head hash is placed on the LP as a lowercase hex string (same convention as binary_encoding in chain-entries.json). Numbers (chain_head_seq) are decimal-stringified. Timestamps and nonces are not part of the signed payload (§6.6 — the semantics are attribution, not a freshness proof)",
  "chain_reference": "chain-entries.json: project_id = genesis entry hash, chain_head_hash_hex = entries[chain_head_seq - 1].entry_hash_hex, attester keys = keys",
  "distribution_note": "removed-attester-in-tenure is a positive case that passes the §6.6 checks (signature, membership at the attested head), but because the attester is not a current member it is outside distribution scope (the server deletes attestation rows when accepting remove_member — §6.4), and even if distributed the client does not use it as verification material (§6.6 (1)). This current-member check is outside this file's verification vectors (implementation test — session-27 §13-5)",
